      "id": "table-10",
      "line": 328,
      "heading_context": "## Common Confusion Points",
      "headers": [
        "Confusion",
        "Correction"
      ],
      "rows": [
        [
          "\"Rust generics are like Java generics.\"",
          "Rust usually monomorphizes; Java mostly erases."
        ],
        [
          "\"`dyn Trait` is slower Rust generics.\"",
          "It is a different representation and dispatch model, chosen explicitly."
        ],
        [
          "\"A vtable layout description is an ABI guarantee.\"",
          "No. Layout is rustc-internal and can change."
        ],
        [
          "\"More codegen units always make builds better.\"",
          "More CGUs can reduce optimization quality; measure per profile."
        ],
        [
          "\"Polymorphization removes generic bloat.\"",
          "Rustc removed that optimization; inspect actual mono items and backend/linker output instead."
        ],
        [
          "\"Cargo decides monomorphization.\"",
          "Cargo schedules crates and passes flags; rustc collects and emits mono items."
        ]
      ]
    },
